menu "Status LED"

config AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED
    bool "Onboard RGB LED shows Core-1 (render) load"
    default y
    help
        Drives the board's onboard addressable RGB LED (WS2812) as a
        render-load indicator. Core-1 busy share maps to color bands:
        green < 50%, yellow >= 50%, orange >= 75%, red >= 90%, with
        hysteresis at the band edges. The LED is only rewritten when the
        band changes, so steady-state cost is one load sample per period.

        The load metric is core_load_sample() in the diagnostics
        component: idle-hook invocation counting, one counter increment
        per idle-loop pass - no kernel critical sections. (Its
        uxTaskGetSystemState() predecessor masked interrupts for the task
        walk and caused 1-2 ms USB audio holes on the 1 s sample grid;
        see core_load.h. This option no longer selects any FreeRTOS
        stats machinery.)

config AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED_GPIO
    int "LED data GPIO"
    depends on AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED
    default 48
    help
        Data line of the onboard addressable LED. ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1
        v1.0 boards route it to GPIO48, v1.1 boards to GPIO38.

config AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED_BRIGHTNESS
    int "Brightness (1-255)"
    depends on AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED
    range 1 255
    default 12
    help
        Full-scale color values are scaled by BRIGHTNESS/255 before being
        written to the LED. Keep low: the onboard LED is bright, and very
        low values (< ~8) start to lose the yellow/orange distinction to
        8-bit channel quantization.

config AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED_PERIOD_MS
    int "Load sample period (ms)"
    depends on AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED
    range 200 5000
    default 1000
    help
        Interval between core-load samples. The displayed load is the mean
        over this window (spikes shorter than the window average out; use
        the render_stats diagnostic for per-block spike analysis).

config AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED_ALLOC_BLINK
    bool "Blink on failed heap allocation"
    depends on AMYSYNTH_STATUS_LED
    default y
    help
        Registers heap_caps_register_failed_alloc_callback() and answers
        any failed allocation with a short magenta blink burst before the
        LED returns to the load color. Note the callback fires on EVERY
        failed alloc, including the first leg of deliberate
        internal-then-PSRAM fallback paths, so an occasional blink can be
        a graceful degrade rather than a hard OOM.

endmenu
